this came as senate republicans  officially released  their version of a coronavirus stimulus  plan  while it includes a second round of  twelve hundred dollar payments  it would only extend additional  unemployment payments by  two hundred dollars a week through  september  that's compared to the current payment  of 600 dollars  starting in october a worker's lost  wages would be covered up to 70 percent  joining us now from capitol hill is new  york senator and democratic minority  leader chuck schumer  senator good morning negotiations with  negotiations with the white house  started last night  u and house speaker nancy pelosi were  there  where do we stand right now well  unfortunately we're pretty far apart  right now although i'm optimistic we  could have a good  solution at the end here's where we are  now we democrats have put together a  package that is bold and strong  and deals with the average needs of  people we don't let them get kicked out  of their homes because they've lost  their job through no fault to their own  we give them a good amount of  unemployment insurance so they can pay  we put in money to feed kids we put in  money to open schools  safely people want schools open but it  has to be done  safely and we give money to state and  local governments because  thousands hundreds of thousands of  firefighters and bus drivers and garbage  workers will be laid off  the republican plan does almost none of  these things  it is stingy it doesn't provide any  money  for instance for more food for people  who need to feed their kids  it provides their unemployment insurance  you're telling people who lost their  jobs through no fault of their own they  get a 30 percent pay cut  it does nothing for state and local  governments is woefully inadequate in  helping our schools open  instead anthony amazingly it has all  these corporate benefits  no money for food stamps but a deduction  for a three martini lunch for a big  businessman  big cushion for defense contractors no  cushion for people who'd be kicked out  of their house and to boot  they threw in there president trump  wants the fbi headquarters built near  his hotel so no new competing hotel  could come in  two billion dollars for that so the  bottom line is and one more point  half the republicans of the senate even  think that's too generous  so we're pretty far apart and the  negotiations were disappointing  yeah so senator i mean the supplemental  benefit uh  unemployment benefit has already run out  for a lot of people it's due to run out  for a lot more by the end of the week um  so  if you're this far apart what are the  what's the real hope here of getting a  deal  so these people aren't in a panic as our  david begna reported from florida  even if if you did the republican plan  most states said unemployment benefits  would be cut off anyway because it's a  whole new plan and they have to readjust  their computers hire new people  many states say it would take months  before people would get their checks  there's a simple solution  the house has passed and we sent it  democrat support simply extending the  existing six hundred dollars a month  until january that could go into effect  easy  that can help our economy because it  puts monies money's money in people's  pockets and then they buy things and go  to the stores that's the only thing  that's kept the economy going  and we can get it done but senator we  urge we urge our republican colleagues  you know in the last two bills  the last two covet bills they were very  stingy we democrats said it had to be  better  and they came in our direction i'm  hopeful that will happen again  the republican argument senator as you  know is that the 600  supplemental is essentially not an  incentive for people to go back to work  it's actually keeping them from going  back to work  that misreads the american people people  want jobs they want permanent jobs they  don't want to stay on unemployment  and the 